<p>Mexico&#x27;s navy has launched a search-and-rescue operation in the Caribbean after two sailboats carrying humanitarian aid left Isla Mujeres, Quintana Roo, on March 20 for Havana and did not arrive on schedule. CBS and the BBC said the missing vessels were part of a broader activist effort involving several countries to send food and other supplies from Mexican ports to Cuba, where shortages of basic goods have added to an already serious humanitarian strain.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/4AslrDFmk5T84xKzrxQN3ubR8BrZnJ5nsic98Zyta0An6pR-SnFoIMqpVXI64SAldk5fVhENVwFguNO_n7d_LTdWlkhsbORmEe8C4JhhkkCc50gJxVvu9pYQL0nBAMbCsIUb1yVXFKgaMbUvwn_16Sb29g-wQFbjHh6UJ4-IJ8P8Et7QtW_wZpAa6bpWp_7BoSTc3sra8nz2GEGVUFU8Do0jWKHx-o7SNYQCBAl5Zkq7Fjk3MCb_UlG_6oNfSilwTPfb0CQm' alt='Two humanitarian aid boats bound for Cuba were reported missing after departing Mexico.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Crew makeup: Officials said nine people of different nationalities were aboard the two aid sailboats when they left Mexico.</li><li>Arrival window: The navy said the vessels were due in Havana on Tuesday or Wednesday before they were reported overdue.</li><li>Search scope: Mexico&#x27;s navy said it alerted naval commanders in the surrounding area, suggesting the response expanded beyond a single patrol zone.</li><li>Vessel type: Reuters and The Guardian described the missing craft as sailboats, not larger cargo vessels.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Mexico&#x27;s navy: The navy said it had received no communication from the boats and no confirmation that they had reached Cuba. As the case escalated, it alerted naval commanders in the surrounding area. (<a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/two-humanitarian-aid-boats-en-route-cuba-missing-mexico-says-2026-03-27/'>Reuters</a>, <a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3348065/mexicos-navy-searches-2-cuba-bound-aid-boats-are-missing'>SCMP</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/two-aid-boats-go-missing-en-route-to-cuba-says-mexico/a-76555529'>Two aid boats go missing en route to Cuba, says Mexico</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3348065/mexicos-navy-searches-2-cuba-bound-aid-boats-are-missing'>Mexico’s navy searches for 2 Cuba-bound aid boats that are missing</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/27/cuba-humanitarian-aid-boats-missing'>Two humanitarian aid boats heading to Cuba have gone missing, Mexico says</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/2-boats-carrying-aid-to-cuba-reported-missing-by-mexico/'>2 boats carrying aid to Cuba reported missing by Mexico</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/3/27/mexico-launches-search-for-two-missing-aid-boats-bound-for-cuba'>Mexico launches search for two missing aid boats bound for Cuba</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/two-humanitarian-aid-boats-en-route-to-cuba-missing-mexico-says'>Two humanitarian aid boats en route to Cuba are missing, Mexico says</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cp84kw1y337o'>Two Cuba-bound aid ships missing after leaving Mexico</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/two-mexican-humanitarian-aid-boats-en-route-to-cuba-missing/article70790969.ece'>Two Mexican humanitarian aid boats en-route to Cuba missing</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/two-humanitarian-aid-boats-en-route-cuba-missing-mexico-says-2026-03-27/'>Mexico&#x27;s navy launches a search and rescue operation in the Caribbean Sea for two sailboats, which departed from Isla Mujeres with nine crew members, carrying humanitarian aid to Cuba after they failed to arrive in Havana as scheduled and lost communication.</a> - reuters.com</li></ul>